Here are concrete Java DSL examples for Option B (`GRID_COLUMNS`/`GRID_ROWS` wire props, `WIDTH`/`HEIGHT` universal again), alongside the SwiftUI/Compose forms they mirror.

## LazyVGrid (fixed columns — the common case)

```java
// auto-fit columns (absent count) — SwiftUI LazyVGrid(.adaptive) / Compose Adaptive
LazyVGrid.of(
    Text.of("A"), Text.of("B"), Text.of("C"), Text.of("D")
);

// 2 equal 1fr columns — SwiftUI LazyVGrid(columns: [GridItem(.flexible())…]) / Compose GridCells.Fixed(2)
LazyVGrid.of(2,
    Text.of("A"), Text.of("B"), Text.of("C"), Text.of("D")
);

// 2 columns + alignment + spacing
LazyVGrid.of(2, Alignment.LEADING, 8f,
    Text.of("A"), Text.of("B"), Text.of("C"), Text.of("D")
);
```

New overloads (existing `of(View...)` / `of(Alignment, float, View...)` stay):
```java
public static LazyVGrid of(int columns, View... children)
public static LazyVGrid of(int columns, Alignment alignment, float spacing, View... children)
```

## LazyHGrid (fixed rows — mirrored)

```java
// 3 rows, cells flow column-major — Compose LazyHorizontalGrid(GridCells.Fixed(3))
LazyHGrid.of(3, Text.of("A"), Text.of("B"), Text.of("C"), Text.of("D"), Text.of("E"), Text.of("F"));
```

## Grid (static) — the open question

SwiftUI's `Grid` takes **no count** (auto). The handoff's model lets the static grid carry counts too (eager `LazyVGrid`-with-count). Three possible Java surfaces:

```java
// (a) SwiftUI-Grid parity: auto-fit only — no count args
Grid.of(Text.of("A"), Text.of("B"), Text.of("C"));

// (b) columns only (eager LazyVGrid)
Grid.of(2, Text.of("A"), Text.of("B"), Text.of("C"));

// (c) columns AND rows (full 2D matrix)
Grid.of(2, 3, Text.of("A"), Text.of("B"), Text.of("C"), Text.of("D"), Text.of("E"), Text.of("F"));
```

Java has no named args, so `Grid.of(2, 3, …)` is positional (columns, rows) — workable but the first two ints read a bit opaquely; (b) avoids that by exposing only `columns`.

## What this means on the wire

- `GRID_COLUMNS` (`0x001E`) set when `columns:` given; `GRID_ROWS` (`0x001F`) when `rows:` given; absent = auto-fit. Emitted as F32 (positive = count; `FILL` = auto-fit + expand).
- `WIDTH`/`HEIGHT` stop being grid counts → `.with(FrameMod.of(200, 200))` on a grid becomes a 200px box (SwiftUI/Compose parity). My in-flight "grid no-px" renderer logic reverts to normal `WIDTH` handling + the new property reads.
- `alignment`/`spacing` constructor args stay exactly as today.

Which static-`Grid` surface do you want — (a) auto-fit only, (b) columns-only, or (c) columns+rows?

