//! # pathland-icons
//!
//! The **canonical icon catalog** for the Pathland `ICON` primitive
//! (spec/ICONS.md): a curated set of **neutral, semantic names** written once in
//! the UI model and mapped by each renderer onto its **native icon set** —
//! Adwaita/freedesktop symbolic icons on GTK, the Lucide set on the web (inline
//! SVG, single-sourced here so SSR and the DOM client agree).
//!
//! The catalog is `no_std` const data only. It is the **single source of truth**
//! for:
//!
//! - the canonical vocabulary (`CATALOG`, [`::names`]),
//! - the GTK icon-theme name ([`gtk_icon_name`]),
//! - the Lucide icon id + inline SVG markup ([`lucide_id`], [`lucide_svg`]) —
//!   also emitted to the DOM client by `pathland-ts-codegen` as
//!   `generated/icons.ts`.
//!
//! Adding an icon = adding one catalog row (+ a Lucide SVG + a GTK name), then
//! regenerating. Unknown names (an app-authored extension) resolve to
//! renderer fallbacks: [`gtk_fallback`] on GTK, an empty-slot placeholder on the
//! web.

